##DESCRIPTION
##  Mental Math problems using (a+1)(a-1)=a^2-1
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('mental math', 'compatible numbers')

## DBsubject('Arithmetic')
## DBchapter('Integers')
## DBsection('Mental Math')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')
## Date('5/3/2020')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGML.pl');

Context('LimitedNumeric');

@a = random_subset(5, 11 .. 20);
@b = map { $_ - 2 } @a;
@c = map { $_ + 2 } @a;

BEGIN_PGML

First, if needed, review the squares up to 20.  Using the square and the identity [`  (a+2)(a-2) = a^2-4 `] to calculate the following mentally

a)  [` [$b[0]] \times [$c[0]] = `] [__]{Compute($b[0]*$c[0])}
b)  [` [$b[1]] \times [$c[1]] = `] [__]{Compute($b[1]*$c[1])}
c)  [` [$b[2]] \times [$c[2]] = `] [__]{Compute($b[2]*$c[2])}
d)  [` [$b[3]] \times [$c[3]] = `] [__]{Compute($b[3]*$c[3])}
e)  [` [$b[4]] \times [$c[4]] = `] [__]{Compute($b[4]*$c[4])}


END_PGML

$sq_tab = DataTable([
    map { $s = $_ * $_; [ PGML("[`$_ \times $_ = $s `]") ] } (12 .. 20) ]);

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

First, recall the squares up to 20:

[$sq_tab]*

Then, mentally the identity [`(a+2)(a-2) = a^2-4`] is used for each:

a)  [` [$b[0]] \times [$c[0]] = [$b[0]+2]^2 -4 = [@($b[0]+2)**2@] -4 = [$b[0]*$c[0]]`]
b)  [` [$b[1]] \times [$c[1]] = [$b[1]+2]^2 -4 = [@($b[1]+2)**2@] -4 =[$b[1]*$c[1]]`]
c)  [` [$b[2]] \times [$c[2]] = [$b[2]+2]^2 -4 = [@($b[2]+2)**2@] -4 =[$b[2]*$c[2]]`]
d)  [` [$b[3]] \times [$c[3]] = [$b[3]+2]^2 -4 = [@($b[3]+2)**2@] -4 =[$b[3]*$c[3]]`]
e)  [` [$b[4]] \times [$c[4]] = [$b[4]+2]^2 -4 = [@($b[4]+2)**2@] -4 =[$b[4]*$c[4]]`]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
